Now Zhuanyu —
in former days the former kings made it master of Dongmeng;
moreover it lies within the bounds of the state;
it is a servant of the altars of soil and grain.
What use is there in attacking it?

Ran You said:
“Our master wants it;
we two servants, neither of us wants it.”

I, Qiu, have heard that those who hold a state or hold a house
do not fret over being few, but fret over not being even;
do not fret over being poor, but fret over not being settled.
For, even, there is no poverty;
at ease, there is no fewness;
settled, there is no toppling.

Now Yóu and Qiu,
you assist your master;
people far off do not submit, and you cannot bring them;
the state divides, crumbles, comes apart and splits, and you cannot hold it;

Kongzi said:
“When the world has the Way, then
the rites and music and the campaigns and attacks issue from the Son of Heaven;
when the world lacks the Way, then
the rites and music and the campaigns and attacks issue from the feudal lords.
When they issue from the feudal lords, likely in ten generations few fail to lose them;
when they issue from the grandees, in five generations few fail to lose them;
when household retainers hold the state's commands, in three generations few fail to lose them.”

Kongzi said:
“Salary has been gone from the ducal house five generations now;
government has come down to the grandees four generations now;
and so those sons and grandsons of the Three Huan are dwindling.”

Kongzi said:
“Attending on a gentleman, there are three errors:
the talk not yet come to you, and speaking — call it haste;
the talk come to you, and not speaking — call it hiding;
not yet seeing his face, and speaking — call it blindness.”

Kongzi said:
“The gentleman has three things to guard against:
in the time of youth, blood and breath not yet settled, guarding against it lies in women;
when he reaches his prime, blood and breath just then hard and strong, guarding against it lies in fighting;
when he reaches old age, blood and breath already failing, guarding against it lies in getting.”

The small man does not know the decree of Heaven and does not hold it in awe;
he takes liberties with great men;
he makes game of the words of the sages.

Kongzi said:
“Those who know it from birth are the highest;
those who know it by learning are next;
stuck, and then learning it, comes after that;
stuck and not learning — the common folk thereby count as the lowest.”

Kongzi said:
“The gentleman has nine thoughts:
looking, he thinks of seeing clear; listening, of hearing keen;
in his look, he thinks of mildness; in his bearing, of respect;
speaking, he thinks of wholeheartedness; at work, of reverent care;
in doubt, he thinks of asking; in anger, of the trouble to follow;
seeing gain, he thinks of what is right.”

Duke Jing of Qi had horses, a thousand teams of four;
on the day he died, the people had no virtue to praise him for.
Boyi and Shuqi starved at the foot of Shouyang;
the people down to now praise them.

The wife of the ruler of a state:
the ruler calls her “the Lady”;
the Lady calls herself “Little Child”;
the people of the state call her “the Lord's Lady”;
speaking of her to other states, they call her “the Little Lord of Scant Virtue”;
the people of other states also call her “the Lord's Lady”.
